## 2. Working with Cubes & Data

### Reading Data (MDX)
Execute native TM1 MDX queries to pull multidimensional cell data into Python.
```python
mdx = """
SELECT 
    {[Period].[Jan], [Period].[Feb]} ON COLUMNS,
    {[Account].[Revenue], [Account].[Net Income]} ON ROWS
FROM [Finance]
WHERE ([Version].[Actual])
"""
# Extract cell data as a native dictionary
data = tm1.cubes.cells.execute_mdx(mdx)
```

### Writing Data to Cells
Write values back to specific coordinates using a dictionary mapping coordinate tuples to values.
```python
cells = {
    ("Actual", "Jan", "Revenue"): 150000,
    ("Actual", "Feb", "Revenue"): 175000
}
tm1.cubes.cells.write_values(cube_name="Finance", cell_dict=cells)
```

